    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d901">

                <pb facs="1410" n="1396" xml:id="pg1396"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00116 EW/11–2944: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-12-02T13:00:00-04:00">December 2, 1944—1
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>10093. Question referred to in your despatch no. 18981<anchor n="28a"
                        xml:id="d901-f1"/> considered by this Department and the War Department to
                    be one having important implications. Your 10541, November 29, 7 p.m.<anchor
                        n="29" xml:id="d901-f2"/> It may be impossible to send Pell instructions
                    before December 6. We would prefer to have vote on matter postponed by
                    Commission beyond December 6 for substantial length of time if possible.<anchor
                        n="30" xml:id="d901-f3"/> Matter is being actively considered by interested
                    Departments here in connection with other related questions. Please repeat to
                    Pell.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stettinius</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d901-f1" n="28a" xml:id="d901-f1-content">
                <p>Dated November 2, <ref target="#pg1391">p. 1391</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d901-f2" n="29" xml:id="d901-f2-content">
                <p>Not printed; it reported that the vote referred to in Department’s telegram 9920,
                    November 25, to London, had been deferred to December 6 (740.00116
                    EW/11–2944).</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d901-f3" n="30" xml:id="d901-f3-content">
                <p>At the 41st meeting of the Commission, December 6, 1944, it was decided that “the
                    subject would be adjourned until the members were ready to take it up again.”
                    (740.00116 European War/12–1144)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
